IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `epd-nouns`
IMPORT `epd-seat-provider`

-- CASES for the provider's seat (epd-seat-provider.l4). Every question has at least one case; the expected value of each was decided
-- from the text of the Directive before the run, and the reason is written above the assertion. Every call names its arguments.

§ `Is the Directive on me? (Articles 2 and 3)`
-- P1: Does the Directive apply to the processing I carry out (Art 3)?
-- Personal data, public service, public network, in the Community.
#ASSERT (`Does the Directive apply to the processing I carry out` WITH `I process personal data` IS TRUE, `it is in connection with a publicly available electronic communications service I provide` IS TRUE, `my network is a public communications network` IS TRUE, `my network is in the Community` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A private network: Art 3 is silent.
#ASSERT (`Does the Directive apply to the processing I carry out` WITH `I process personal data` IS TRUE, `it is in connection with a publicly available electronic communications service I provide` IS TRUE, `my network is a public communications network` IS FALSE, `my network is in the Community` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- P2: Is my service a "value added service" (Art 2(g))?
-- A service that needs extra traffic data: Art 2(g) "means".
#ASSERT (`Is my service a value added service` WITH `my service needs more traffic data than conveying and billing need` IS TRUE, `my service needs more location data than conveying and billing need` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Needs neither: not a value added service.
#ASSERT (`Is my service a value added service` WITH `my service needs more traffic data than conveying and billing need` IS FALSE, `my service needs more location data than conveying and billing need` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Security and breaches (Article 4)`
-- P3: Have I taken the security measures Art 4(1) requires?
-- Measures taken; no need to act with the network provider.
#ASSERT (`Have I taken the security measures Article 4(1) requires` WITH `I have taken appropriate technical and organisational measures` IS TRUE, `I need to act together with the network provider` IS FALSE, `I have acted together with the network provider` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Acting with the network provider was necessary, and I did not.
#ASSERT (`Have I taken the security measures Article 4(1) requires` WITH `I have taken appropriate technical and organisational measures` IS TRUE, `I need to act together with the network provider` IS TRUE, `I have acted together with the network provider` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P4: Do my measures include at least what Art 4(1a) requires?
-- All three dashes present.
#ASSERT (`Do my measures include at least what Article 4(1a) requires` WITH `my measures limit access to authorised staff for lawful purposes` IS TRUE, `my measures protect data against loss, alteration and unauthorised processing` IS TRUE, `I have a security policy` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No security policy: the measures "shall at least" include one.
#ASSERT (`Do my measures include at least what Article 4(1a) requires` WITH `my measures limit access to authorised staff for lawful purposes` IS TRUE, `my measures protect data against loss, alteration and unauthorised processing` IS TRUE, `I have a security policy` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P5: Must I warn my subscribers of a particular risk to the security of the network (Art 4(2))?
-- In case of a particular risk the provider must inform the subscribers.
#ASSERT (`Must I warn my subscribers of a particular risk to the security of the network` WITH `there is a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No such risk: "In case of a particular risk" is not met.
#ASSERT (`Must I warn my subscribers of a particular risk to the security of the network` WITH `there is a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P6: Have I warned my subscribers as Art 4(2) requires?
-- Told of the risk; the risk is within my own measures, so no remedies need be listed.
#ASSERT (`Have I warned my subscribers as Article 4(2) requires` WITH `I told my subscribers of the risk` IS TRUE, `the risk is outside my own measures` IS FALSE, `I told them of the remedies and likely costs` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The risk is outside my measures and I did not tell them the remedies and likely costs.
#ASSERT (`Have I warned my subscribers as Article 4(2) requires` WITH `I told my subscribers of the risk` IS TRUE, `the risk is outside my own measures` IS TRUE, `I told them of the remedies and likely costs` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P7: Must I notify the authority of this personal data breach (Art 4(3))?
-- In the case of a personal data breach: notify the competent national authority.
#ASSERT (`Must I notify the authority of this personal data breach` WITH `there has been a personal data breach` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No breach: "In the case of a personal data breach" is not met.
#ASSERT (`Must I notify the authority of this personal data breach` WITH `there has been a personal data breach` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P8: Have I notified the authority in time (Art 4(3))?
-- Notified without undue delay.
#ASSERT (`Have I notified the authority in time` WITH `I notified the authority` IS TRUE, `I did it without undue delay` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Notified, but with undue delay.
#ASSERT (`Have I notified the authority in time` WITH `I notified the authority` IS TRUE, `I did it without undue delay` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P9: Must I also notify the subscriber or individual affected (Art 4(3))?
-- A breach likely to adversely affect a subscriber: also notify them.
#ASSERT (`Must I also notify the subscriber or individual affected` WITH `there has been a personal data breach` IS TRUE, `it is likely to harm the subscriber's or individual's data or privacy` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A breach not likely to affect them adversely: the "when" gate fails.
#ASSERT (`Must I also notify the subscriber or individual affected` WITH `there has been a personal data breach` IS TRUE, `it is likely to harm the subscriber's or individual's data or privacy` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P10: Have I notified the subscriber or individual in time (Art 4(3))?
-- Notified without undue delay.
#ASSERT (`Have I notified the subscriber or individual in time` WITH `I notified the subscriber or individual` IS TRUE, `I did it without undue delay` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not notified.
#ASSERT (`Have I notified the subscriber or individual in time` WITH `I notified the subscriber or individual` IS FALSE, `I did it without undue delay` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P11: Am I excused from notifying the subscriber because I protected the data (Art 4(3))?
-- Excused: "shall not be required if the provider has demonstrated ... appropriate technological protection measures" that were applied and render the data unintelligible.
#ASSERT (`Am I excused from notifying the subscriber because I protected the data` WITH `I have shown the authority I had appropriate protection measures` IS TRUE, `those measures covered the data in the breach` IS TRUE, `they make the data unintelligible to anyone unauthorised` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not demonstrated to the authority: the sentence says when notification is not required, not that it is required.
#ASSERT (`Am I excused from notifying the subscriber because I protected the data` WITH `I have shown the authority I had appropriate protection measures` IS FALSE, `those measures covered the data in the breach` IS TRUE, `they make the data unintelligible to anyone unauthorised` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- P12: May the authority require me to notify the subscriber or individual (Art 4(3))?
-- Not yet notified, and the authority has considered the likely adverse effects: it "may require" me to do so.
#ASSERT (`May the authority require me to notify the subscriber or individual` WITH `I have not yet notified the subscriber or individual` IS TRUE, `the authority has considered the likely adverse effects` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Already notified: a power whose gate failed.
#ASSERT (`May the authority require me to notify the subscriber or individual` WITH `I have not yet notified the subscriber or individual` IS FALSE, `the authority has considered the likely adverse effects` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- P13: Does my notice to the subscriber say what Art 4(3) requires?
-- All three.
#ASSERT (`Does my notice to the subscriber say what Article 4(3) requires` WITH `it describes the nature of the breach` IS TRUE, `it gives contact points` IS TRUE, `it recommends measures to limit the harm` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No recommended measures.
#ASSERT (`Does my notice to the subscriber say what Article 4(3) requires` WITH `it describes the nature of the breach` IS TRUE, `it gives contact points` IS TRUE, `it recommends measures to limit the harm` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P14: Does my notice to the authority say what Art 4(3) requires?
-- All five elements.
#ASSERT (`Does my notice to the authority say what Article 4(3) requires` WITH `it describes the nature of the breach` IS TRUE, `it gives contact points` IS TRUE, `it recommends measures to limit the harm` IS TRUE, `it describes the consequences` IS TRUE, `it describes what I have done or propose to do` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The consequences are not described.
#ASSERT (`Does my notice to the authority say what Article 4(3) requires` WITH `it describes the nature of the breach` IS TRUE, `it gives contact points` IS TRUE, `it recommends measures to limit the harm` IS TRUE, `it describes the consequences` IS FALSE, `it describes what I have done or propose to do` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P15: May the authority adopt guidelines or give me instructions on how I must notify breaches (Art 4(4))?
-- A guideline on the format of notifications.
#ASSERT (`May the authority adopt guidelines or give me instructions on notifying breaches` WITH `it is about when I must notify, the format or the manner` IS TRUE, `it is an instruction` IS FALSE, `the instruction is necessary` IS FALSE, `technical implementing measures under paragraph 5 cover the point` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An instruction that is not necessary: "where necessary, issue instructions".
#ASSERT (`May the authority adopt guidelines or give me instructions on notifying breaches` WITH `it is about when I must notify, the format or the manner` IS TRUE, `it is an instruction` IS TRUE, `the instruction is necessary` IS FALSE, `technical implementing measures under paragraph 5 cover the point` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Technical implementing measures under paragraph 5 cover it: their content is outside the sources.
#ASSERT (`May the authority adopt guidelines or give me instructions on notifying breaches` WITH `it is about when I must notify, the format or the manner` IS TRUE, `it is an instruction` IS FALSE, `the instruction is necessary` IS FALSE, `technical implementing measures under paragraph 5 cover the point` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- P16: Is my inventory of personal data breaches as Art 4(4) requires?
-- All five.
#ASSERT (`Is my inventory of personal data breaches as Article 4(4) requires` WITH `it records the facts` IS TRUE, `it records the effects` IS TRUE, `it records the remedial action taken` IS TRUE, `it is enough for the authority to check my compliance` IS TRUE, `it holds only what is needed for that` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- It includes more than the information necessary.
#ASSERT (`Is my inventory of personal data breaches as Article 4(4) requires` WITH `it records the facts` IS TRUE, `it records the effects` IS TRUE, `it records the remedial action taken` IS TRUE, `it is enough for the authority to check my compliance` IS TRUE, `it holds only what is needed for that` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P17: Must the authority impose sanctions on me if I failed to notify (Art 4(4))?
-- "shall impose appropriate sanctions in the event of a failure to do so".
#ASSERT (`Must the authority impose sanctions on me if I failed to notify` WITH `I failed to comply with my notification obligations` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No failure: "in the event of a failure" is not met.
#ASSERT (`Must the authority impose sanctions on me if I failed to notify` WITH `I failed to comply with my notification obligations` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Confidentiality and traffic data (Articles 5 and 6)`
-- P18: Must interception of my customers' communications be prohibited, including by me (Art 5(1))?
-- Interception by a person other than a user, without consent or authority.
#ASSERT (`Must interception of my customers' communications be prohibited including by me` WITH `it is listening, tapping, storage, interception or surveillance` IS TRUE, `it is of communications or related traffic data` IS TRUE, `it is by someone other than a user` IS TRUE, `the users concerned consented` IS FALSE, `it is legally authorised under Article 15(1)` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Legally authorised in accordance with Article 15(1).
#ASSERT (`Must interception of my customers' communications be prohibited including by me` WITH `it is listening, tapping, storage, interception or surveillance` IS TRUE, `it is of communications or related traffic data` IS TRUE, `it is by someone other than a user` IS TRUE, `the users concerned consented` IS FALSE, `it is legally authorised under Article 15(1)` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P19: Does the confidentiality rule stop me storing data technically needed to carry a communication (Art 5(1))?
-- "This paragraph shall not prevent technical storage which is necessary for the conveyance of a communication".
#ASSERT (`Does the confidentiality rule stop me storing data technically needed to carry a communication` WITH `the storage is technical and necessary for the conveyance` IS TRUE, `it is without prejudice to confidentiality` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not needed for conveyance: the sentence is silent.
#ASSERT (`Does the confidentiality rule stop me storing data technically needed to carry a communication` WITH `the storage is technical and necessary for the conveyance` IS FALSE, `it is without prejudice to confidentiality` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- P20: May I record communications in the course of lawful business to prove a transaction (Art 5(2))?
-- Yes, I may: authorised, in lawful business practice, to prove a transaction, so "Paragraph 1 shall not affect" the recording.
#ASSERT (`May I record communications in the course of lawful business to prove a transaction` WITH `the recording is legally authorised` IS TRUE, `it is of communications and related traffic data` IS TRUE, `it is in the course of lawful business practice` IS TRUE, `it is to provide evidence of a business transaction` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not for that purpose: the paragraph is silent.
#ASSERT (`May I record communications in the course of lawful business to prove a transaction` WITH `the recording is legally authorised` IS TRUE, `it is of communications and related traffic data` IS TRUE, `it is in the course of lawful business practice` IS TRUE, `it is to provide evidence of a business transaction` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- P21: Do I need consent to store information on, or read it from, a subscriber's device (Art 5(3))?
-- It is "only allowed on condition that the subscriber or user concerned has given his or her consent".
#ASSERT (`Do I need consent to store information on or read it from a subscribers device` WITH `it is storing or gaining access to information in the terminal equipment` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not storage in or access to the terminal equipment: silent.
#ASSERT (`Do I need consent to store information on or read it from a subscribers device` WITH `it is storing or gaining access to information in the terminal equipment` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- P22: Have I met the condition of consent for what I store on, or read from, a device (Art 5(3))?
-- Consent and information in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC.
#ASSERT (`Have I met the condition of consent for what I store on or read from a device` WITH `the subscriber gave consent` IS TRUE, `I gave clear and comprehensive information` IS TRUE, `the consent and information meet Directive 95/46/EC` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No consent.
#ASSERT (`Have I met the condition of consent for what I store on or read from a device` WITH `the subscriber gave consent` IS FALSE, `I gave clear and comprehensive information` IS TRUE, `the consent and information meet Directive 95/46/EC` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P23: Does the consent rule stop storage or access that is strictly necessary for a service the user requested (Art 5(3))?
-- Technical storage strictly necessary for a service the user explicitly requested.
#ASSERT (`Does the consent rule stop storage strictly necessary for a service the user requested` WITH `it is technical storage or access` IS TRUE, `it is for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication` IS FALSE, `the user explicitly requested the service` IS TRUE, `it is strictly necessary for that service` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not strictly necessary: the sentence is silent.
#ASSERT (`Does the consent rule stop storage strictly necessary for a service the user requested` WITH `it is technical storage or access` IS TRUE, `it is for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication` IS FALSE, `the user explicitly requested the service` IS TRUE, `it is strictly necessary for that service` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- P24: Must I erase this traffic data or make it anonymous (Art 6(1))?
-- Traffic data no longer needed for transmission, and no other rule applies.
#ASSERT (`Must I erase this traffic data or make it anonymous` WITH `it is traffic data I process and store` IS TRUE, `I no longer need it to carry the communication` IS TRUE, `another rule applies to it` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Still needed for transmission.
#ASSERT (`Must I erase this traffic data or make it anonymous` WITH `it is traffic data I process and store` IS TRUE, `I no longer need it to carry the communication` IS FALSE, `another rule applies to it` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Another rule applies: "without prejudice to paragraphs 2, 3 and 5 ... and Article 15(1)".
#ASSERT (`Must I erase this traffic data or make it anonymous` WITH `it is traffic data I process and store` IS TRUE, `I no longer need it to carry the communication` IS TRUE, `another rule applies to it` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- P25: May I process this traffic data for billing on this date (Art 6(2))?
-- On the last day itself: "only up to the end of the period".
#ASSERT (`May I process this traffic data for billing on this date` WITH `it is data necessary for billing and interconnection payments` IS TRUE, `the date of the processing` IS (Date 31 1 2025), `the last day the bill can be challenged or payment pursued` IS (Date 31 1 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The day after the period ends.
#ASSERT (`May I process this traffic data for billing on this date` WITH `it is data necessary for billing and interconnection payments` IS TRUE, `the date of the processing` IS (Date 1 2 2025), `the last day the bill can be challenged or payment pursued` IS (Date 31 1 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P26: May I process traffic data for marketing or value added services (Art 6(3))?
-- Purpose, prior consent and necessary extent.
#ASSERT (`May I process traffic data for marketing or value added services` WITH `it is for marketing electronic communications services or a value added service` IS TRUE, `the subscriber or user gave prior consent` IS TRUE, `I go no further than the services or marketing need` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No prior consent: a "may" grant whose "if" gate failed.
#ASSERT (`May I process traffic data for marketing or value added services` WITH `it is for marketing electronic communications services or a value added service` IS TRUE, `the subscriber or user gave prior consent` IS FALSE, `I go no further than the services or marketing need` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- P27: Have I told the subscriber or user what Art 6(4) requires about traffic data?
-- Types and duration told, before consent.
#ASSERT (`Have I told the subscriber what Article 6(4) requires about traffic data` WITH `the purpose is marketing or a value added service` IS TRUE, `I told them the types of traffic data` IS TRUE, `I told them how long` IS TRUE, `I told them before obtaining consent` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Told after consent.
#ASSERT (`Have I told the subscriber what Article 6(4) requires about traffic data` WITH `the purpose is marketing or a value added service` IS TRUE, `I told them the types of traffic data` IS TRUE, `I told them how long` IS TRUE, `I told them before obtaining consent` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P28: Is my staff's handling of traffic data restricted as Art 6(5) requires?
-- Under my authority, for fraud detection, no more than necessary.
#ASSERT (`Is my staffs handling of traffic data restricted as Article 6(5) requires` WITH `it is by people under my authority` IS TRUE, `the activity` IS `fraud detection`, `it goes no further than that activity needs` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Beyond what is necessary.
#ASSERT (`Is my staffs handling of traffic data restricted as Article 6(5) requires` WITH `it is by people under my authority` IS TRUE, `the activity` IS `fraud detection`, `it goes no further than that activity needs` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P29: May a competent body be told traffic data to settle a dispute (Art 6(6))?
-- A competent body, lawfully, to settle a billing dispute.
#ASSERT (`May a competent body be told traffic data to settle a dispute` WITH `the body is a competent body` IS TRUE, `it is in conformity with applicable legislation` IS TRUE, `it is to settle disputes` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not for settling a dispute: the clause is silent.
#ASSERT (`May a competent body be told traffic data to settle a dispute` WITH `the body is a competent body` IS TRUE, `it is in conformity with applicable legislation` IS TRUE, `it is to settle disputes` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Line identification, location, and call forwarding (Articles 8 to 11)`
-- P30: Have I given the calling user what Art 8(1) requires?
-- Offered per call, simply and free.
#ASSERT (`Have I given the calling user what Article 8(1) requires` WITH `I offer the calling user the possibility of hiding their number` IS TRUE, `it works call by call` IS TRUE, `it is simple` IS TRUE, `it is free` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not per call.
#ASSERT (`Have I given the calling user what Article 8(1) requires` WITH `I offer the calling user the possibility of hiding their number` IS TRUE, `it works call by call` IS FALSE, `it is simple` IS TRUE, `it is free` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P31: Have I given the called subscriber what Art 8(2) requires?
-- Offered simply and free for reasonable use.
#ASSERT (`Have I given the called subscriber what Article 8(2) requires` WITH `I offer the possibility of blocking presentation of callers' numbers` IS TRUE, `it is simple` IS TRUE, `the use is reasonable` IS TRUE, `it is free` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- For reasonable use it is not free.
#ASSERT (`Have I given the called subscriber what Article 8(2) requires` WITH `I offer the possibility of blocking presentation of callers' numbers` IS TRUE, `it is simple` IS TRUE, `the use is reasonable` IS TRUE, `it is free` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P32: Have I given the called subscriber what Art 8(3) requires?
-- Offered by a simple means.
#ASSERT (`Have I given the called subscriber what Article 8(3) requires` WITH `I offer the possibility of rejecting calls from hidden numbers` IS TRUE, `it is simple` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not offered.
#ASSERT (`Have I given the called subscriber what Article 8(3) requires` WITH `I offer the possibility of rejecting calls from hidden numbers` IS FALSE, `it is simple` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P33: Have I given the called subscriber what Art 8(4) requires?
-- Offered simply and free.
#ASSERT (`Have I given the called subscriber what Article 8(4) requires` WITH `I offer the possibility of hiding the connected line identification` IS TRUE, `it is simple` IS TRUE, `it is free` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not free.
#ASSERT (`Have I given the called subscriber what Article 8(4) requires` WITH `I offer the possibility of hiding the connected line identification` IS TRUE, `it is simple` IS TRUE, `it is free` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P34: Must I tell the public about line identification and the possibilities (Art 8(6))?
-- Where presentation is offered, providers inform the public.
#ASSERT (`Must I tell the public about line identification and the possibilities` WITH `I offer calling or connected line identification` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not offered: the "where" condition fails.
#ASSERT (`Must I tell the public about line identification and the possibilities` WITH `I offer calling or connected line identification` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P35: Have I told the public as Art 8(6) requires?
-- Both.
#ASSERT (`Have I told the public as Article 8(6) requires` WITH `I tell the public that presentation is offered` IS TRUE, `I tell the public of the possibilities in Art 8(1) to (4)` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The possibilities are not explained.
#ASSERT (`Have I told the public as Article 8(6) requires` WITH `I tell the public that presentation is offered` IS TRUE, `I tell the public of the possibilities in Art 8(1) to (4)` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P36: May I process location data (other than traffic data)(Art 9(1))?
-- Made anonymous.
#ASSERT (`May I process location data other than traffic data` WITH `it is location data of users or subscribers of a public network or service` IS TRUE, `I have made it anonymous` IS TRUE, `the users or subscribers consented` IS FALSE, `I go no further than the value added service needs` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither anonymous nor consented: "may only be processed when ...".
#ASSERT (`May I process location data other than traffic data` WITH `it is location data of users or subscribers of a public network or service` IS TRUE, `I have made it anonymous` IS FALSE, `the users or subscribers consented` IS FALSE, `I go no further than the value added service needs` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P37: Have I told users what Art 9(1) requires before asking consent to location processing?
-- All four things, before consent.
#ASSERT (`Have I told users what Article 9(1) requires before asking consent to location processing` WITH `I told them the type of location data` IS TRUE, `I told them the purposes` IS TRUE, `I told them how long` IS TRUE, `I told them whether a third party receives it` IS TRUE, `I told them before obtaining consent` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Told after consent.
#ASSERT (`Have I told users what Article 9(1) requires before asking consent to location processing` WITH `I told them the type of location data` IS TRUE, `I told them the purposes` IS TRUE, `I told them how long` IS TRUE, `I told them whether a third party receives it` IS TRUE, `I told them before obtaining consent` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P38: Do my users have the temporary refusal Art 9(2) requires?
-- All four.
#ASSERT (`Do my users have the temporary refusal Article 9(2) requires` WITH `users can temporarily refuse the processing` IS TRUE, `it is simple` IS TRUE, `it is free` IS TRUE, `it works for each connection or transmission` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not free of charge.
#ASSERT (`Do my users have the temporary refusal Article 9(2) requires` WITH `users can temporarily refuse the processing` IS TRUE, `it is simple` IS TRUE, `it is free` IS FALSE, `it works for each connection or transmission` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P39: Is the handling of location data restricted as Art 9(3) requires?
-- In accordance with paragraphs 1 and 2, by people under my authority, no further than necessary.
#ASSERT (`Is the handling of location data restricted as Article 9(3) requires` WITH `it is in accordance with Art 9(1) and (2)` IS TRUE, `it is by people under my authority` IS TRUE, `it is by people under the value added service provider's authority` IS FALSE, `it goes no further than the value added service needs` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- By people under neither authority.
#ASSERT (`Is the handling of location data restricted as Article 9(3) requires` WITH `it is in accordance with Art 9(1) and (2)` IS TRUE, `it is by people under my authority` IS FALSE, `it is by people under the value added service provider's authority` IS FALSE, `it goes no further than the value added service needs` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P40: May I override a subscriber's hiding of their number to trace malicious calls (Art 10(a))?
-- Temporary, on application, to trace malicious calls.
#ASSERT (`May I override a subscribers hiding of their number to trace malicious calls` WITH `it is an override of hiding the calling number` IS TRUE, `it is temporary` IS TRUE, `the subscriber applied for it` IS TRUE, `it is to trace malicious or nuisance calls` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not on a subscriber's application: outside the clause.
#ASSERT (`May I override a subscribers hiding of their number to trace malicious calls` WITH `it is an override of hiding the calling number` IS TRUE, `it is temporary` IS TRUE, `the subscriber applied for it` IS FALSE, `it is to trace malicious or nuisance calls` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- P41: May I override line identification or location consent for an emergency organisation (Art 10(b))?
-- A recognised emergency organisation, per line, to respond to calls.
#ASSERT (`May I override line identification or location consent for an emergency organisation` WITH `it overrides hiding the number or the denial of location consent` IS TRUE, `it is line by line` IS TRUE, `the organisation deals with emergency calls` IS TRUE, `a Member State recognises it as such` IS TRUE, `it is to respond to emergency calls` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An organisation no Member State recognises: outside the words.
#ASSERT (`May I override line identification or location consent for an emergency organisation` WITH `it overrides hiding the number or the denial of location consent` IS TRUE, `it is line by line` IS TRUE, `the organisation deals with emergency calls` IS TRUE, `a Member State recognises it as such` IS FALSE, `it is to respond to emergency calls` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- P42: Have I given subscribers what Art 11 requires about call forwarding?
-- All three.
#ASSERT (`Have I given subscribers what Article 11 requires about call forwarding` WITH `subscribers can stop automatic call forwarding by a third party` IS TRUE, `it is simple` IS TRUE, `it is free` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not free of charge.
#ASSERT (`Have I given subscribers what Article 11 requires about call forwarding` WITH `subscribers can stop automatic call forwarding by a third party` IS TRUE, `it is simple` IS TRUE, `it is free` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Directories (Article 12)`
-- P43: Have I given subscribers the information Art 12(1) requires before including them in a directory?
-- Everything told, free, before inclusion.
#ASSERT (`Have I given subscribers the information Article 12(1) requires before including them` WITH `I told them the purposes of the directory` IS TRUE, `it has search functions in an electronic version` IS TRUE, `I told them of the further uses` IS TRUE, `I told them free of charge` IS TRUE, `I told them before including them` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Told after inclusion.
#ASSERT (`Have I given subscribers the information Article 12(1) requires before including them` WITH `I told them the purposes of the directory` IS TRUE, `it has search functions in an electronic version` IS TRUE, `I told them of the further uses` IS TRUE, `I told them free of charge` IS TRUE, `I told them before including them` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P44: Have I given subscribers the opportunity Art 12(2) requires?
-- All opportunities given for relevant data.
#ASSERT (`Have I given subscribers the opportunity Article 12(2) requires` WITH `I let them decide whether they are included` IS TRUE, `the data is relevant for the directory's purpose` IS TRUE, `I let them decide which data are included` IS TRUE, `I let them verify it` IS TRUE, `I let them correct it` IS TRUE, `I let them withdraw it` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- They cannot correct the data.
#ASSERT (`Have I given subscribers the opportunity Article 12(2) requires` WITH `I let them decide whether they are included` IS TRUE, `the data is relevant for the directory's purpose` IS TRUE, `I let them decide which data are included` IS TRUE, `I let them verify it` IS TRUE, `I let them correct it` IS FALSE, `I let them withdraw it` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The data is not relevant for the directory's purpose: no choice of "which" is given for it.
#ASSERT (`Have I given subscribers the opportunity Article 12(2) requires` WITH `I let them decide whether they are included` IS TRUE, `the data is relevant for the directory's purpose` IS FALSE, `I let them decide which data are included` IS FALSE, `I let them verify it` IS TRUE, `I let them correct it` IS TRUE, `I let them withdraw it` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- P45: Is not being included in the directory, and checking, correcting or withdrawing data, free for subscribers as Art 12(2) requires?
-- All free.
#ASSERT (`Is not being in the directory and correcting data free for subscribers as Article 12(2) requires` WITH `not being included is free` IS TRUE, `verifying is free` IS TRUE, `correcting is free` IS TRUE, `withdrawing is free` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Withdrawing is charged for.
#ASSERT (`Is not being in the directory and correcting data free for subscribers as Article 12(2) requires` WITH `not being included is free` IS TRUE, `verifying is free` IS TRUE, `correcting is free` IS TRUE, `withdrawing is free` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Proceedings, penalties and my own duties to the authority (Articles 13, 15 and 15a)`
-- P46: May I bring legal proceedings against a sender breaching the marketing rules (Art 13(6))?
-- A provider adversely affected and protecting its legitimate business interests.
#ASSERT (`May I bring legal proceedings against a sender breaching the marketing rules` WITH `I am adversely affected by the infringement` IS TRUE, `I have a legitimate interest in stopping it` IS FALSE, `I am an electronic communications service provider protecting my business interests` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not adversely affected: a power whose gate failed.
#ASSERT (`May I bring legal proceedings against a sender breaching the marketing rules` WITH `I am adversely affected by the infringement` IS FALSE, `I have a legitimate interest in stopping it` IS FALSE, `I am an electronic communications service provider protecting my business interests` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- P47: May the Member State penalise me for negligently contributing to unsolicited-message infringements (Art 13(6))?
-- A provider that by negligence contributes: Member States may lay down specific penalty rules.
#ASSERT (`May the Member State penalise me for negligently contributing to unsolicited message infringements` WITH `I am a provider of electronic communications services` IS TRUE, `I contributed by my negligence` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No negligence: a power whose gate failed.
#ASSERT (`May the Member State penalise me for negligently contributing to unsolicited message infringements` WITH `I am a provider of electronic communications services` IS TRUE, `I contributed by my negligence` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- P48: Have I set up the internal procedures Art 15(1b) requires for access requests?
-- Procedures established.
#ASSERT (`Have I set up the internal procedures Article 15(1b) requires for access requests` WITH `I have internal procedures for responding to requests for access to users' data` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- None: "Providers shall establish internal procedures".
#ASSERT (`Have I set up the internal procedures Article 15(1b) requires for access requests` WITH `I have internal procedures for responding to requests for access to users' data` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P49: Must I give the authority information about my access-request procedures (Art 15(1b))?
-- On demand: provide the information.
#ASSERT (`Must I give the authority information about my access request procedures` WITH `the authority has demanded it` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No demand: "on demand" is not met (a "where"-type condition; fork register).
#ASSERT (`Must I give the authority information about my access request procedures` WITH `the authority has demanded it` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P50: Have I given the authority the information Art 15(1b) requires?
-- All four.
#ASSERT (`Have I given the authority the information Article 15(1b) requires` WITH `I provided information about the procedures` IS TRUE, `I provided the number of requests` IS TRUE, `I provided the legal justification invoked` IS TRUE, `I provided my response` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The legal justification was left out.
#ASSERT (`Have I given the authority the information Article 15(1b) requires` WITH `I provided information about the procedures` IS TRUE, `I provided the number of requests` IS TRUE, `I provided the legal justification invoked` IS FALSE, `I provided my response` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P51: Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to order me, as a provider, to stop an infringement (Art 15a(2))?
-- The competent national authority.
#ASSERT (`Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to order me as a provider to stop an infringement` WITH `it is an infringement of the national rules under this Directive` IS TRUE, `the body is the competent national authority` IS TRUE, `the body is another national body` IS FALSE, `it is relevant for that body to have the power` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not an infringement of the national provisions: the sentence is silent.
#ASSERT (`Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to order me as a provider to stop an infringement` WITH `it is an infringement of the national rules under this Directive` IS FALSE, `the body is the competent national authority` IS TRUE, `the body is another national body` IS FALSE, `it is relevant for that body to have the power` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- P52: Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to require me, as a provider, to give it information when it investigates (Art 15a(3))?
-- The competent national authority must have the power to obtain any relevant information.
#ASSERT (`Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to require me as a provider to give it information when it investigates` WITH `the body is the competent national authority` IS TRUE, `the body is another national body` IS FALSE, `it is relevant for that body to have the powers` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Another body for which it is not relevant: "where relevant".
#ASSERT (`Does the Directive require my Member State to give the authority the power to require me as a provider to give it information when it investigates` WITH `the body is the competent national authority` IS FALSE, `the body is another national body` IS TRUE, `it is relevant for that body to have the powers` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Which of my duties bind me on these facts? ("Must I ...?")`
-- P53: Must I offer the calling user the possibility of hiding their number call by call (Art 8(1))?
-- Where presentation is offered, the provider must offer the calling user the possibility.
#ASSERT (`Must I offer the calling user the possibility of hiding their number call by call` WITH `I offer presentation of calling line identification` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not offered: the "where" condition fails (fork register F6).
#ASSERT (`Must I offer the calling user the possibility of hiding their number call by call` WITH `I offer presentation of calling line identification` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P54: Must I let the called subscriber stop callers' numbers being shown to them (Art 8(2))?
-- Where presentation is offered.
#ASSERT (`Must I let the called subscriber stop callers numbers being shown to them` WITH `I offer presentation of calling line identification` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not offered (fork register F6).
#ASSERT (`Must I let the called subscriber stop callers numbers being shown to them` WITH `I offer presentation of calling line identification` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P55: Must I let the called subscriber reject calls from hidden numbers (Art 8(3))?
-- Both "where" conditions hold.
#ASSERT (`Must I let the called subscriber reject calls from hidden numbers` WITH `I offer presentation of calling line identification` IS TRUE, `I present it before the call is established` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Identification is not presented before the call is established (fork register F6).
#ASSERT (`Must I let the called subscriber reject calls from hidden numbers` WITH `I offer presentation of calling line identification` IS TRUE, `I present it before the call is established` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P56: Must I let the called subscriber hide the connected line identification (Art 8(4))?
-- Where presentation of connected line identification is offered.
#ASSERT (`Must I let the called subscriber hide the connected line identification` WITH `I offer presentation of connected line identification` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not offered (fork register F6).
#ASSERT (`Must I let the called subscriber hide the connected line identification` WITH `I offer presentation of connected line identification` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P57: Must I tell the subscriber or user about the traffic data I process (Art 6(4))?
-- A purpose mentioned in paragraph 2 or 3.
#ASSERT (`Must I tell the subscriber or user about the traffic data I process` WITH `the purpose is billing or interconnection, or marketing or a value added service` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Another purpose: the duty is stated for paragraphs 2 and 3.
#ASSERT (`Must I tell the subscriber or user about the traffic data I process` WITH `the purpose is billing or interconnection, or marketing or a value added service` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- P58: Must I also tell my subscribers of possible remedies and likely costs (Art 4(2))?
-- A particular risk that lies outside my own measures.
#ASSERT (`Must I also tell my subscribers of possible remedies and likely costs` WITH `there is a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network` IS TRUE, `the risk is outside my own measures` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The risk is within my own measures: "where the risk lies outside the scope" is not met.
#ASSERT (`Must I also tell my subscribers of possible remedies and likely costs` WITH `there is a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network` IS TRUE, `the risk is outside my own measures` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P59: Must I tell users before asking their consent to location processing (Art 9(1))?
-- Prior to obtaining consent, inform them.
#ASSERT (`Must I tell users before asking their consent to location processing` WITH `I am asking for their consent to location processing` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No consent is being obtained: the sentence is silent.
#ASSERT (`Must I tell users before asking their consent to location processing` WITH `I am asking for their consent to location processing` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- P60: Must users keep the possibility of temporarily refusing location processing (Art 9(2))?
-- Where consent has been obtained, the possibility must continue.
#ASSERT (`Must users keep the possibility of temporarily refusing location processing` WITH `consent has been obtained for location processing` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No consent obtained: the "where" condition fails (fork register F6).
#ASSERT (`Must users keep the possibility of temporarily refusing location processing` WITH `consent has been obtained for location processing` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P61: Must I set up internal procedures for access requests (Art 15(1b))?
-- Providers shall establish internal procedures.
#ASSERT (`Must I set up internal procedures for access requests` WITH `I am a provider` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a provider: the sentence is silent.
#ASSERT (`Must I set up internal procedures for access requests` WITH `I am a provider` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- P62: May my Member State require me to keep data for a limited period for the State's purposes (Art 15(1))?
-- A legislative measure for a limited period on the grounds in paragraph 1.
#ASSERT (`May my Member State require me to keep data for a limited period` WITH `it is a law requiring retention of data` IS TRUE, `the retention is for a limited period` IS TRUE, `it is justified on the grounds in Art 15(1)` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No limited period: outside the words of the sentence.
#ASSERT (`May my Member State require me to keep data for a limited period` WITH `it is a law requiring retention of data` IS TRUE, `the retention is for a limited period` IS FALSE, `it is justified on the grounds in Art 15(1)` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- P63: May my Member State require additional consent for my directory's other purposes (Art 12(3))?
-- A purpose other than a name search: additional consent may be required.
#ASSERT (`May my Member State require additional consent for my directorys other purposes` WITH `the purpose is other than searching contact details by name` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A name search: a power whose gate failed.
#ASSERT (`May my Member State require additional consent for my directorys other purposes` WITH `the purpose is other than searching contact details by name` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `A few more questions on my duties and the authority's powers (Articles 4, 8 and 10)`
-- P64: Do my security measures ensure a level of security appropriate to the risk (Art 4(1))?
-- The measures ensure an appropriate level: Art 4(1) second sentence is met.
#ASSERT (`Do my security measures ensure a level of security appropriate to the risk` WITH `my measures ensure a level of security appropriate to the risk presented, having regard to the state of the art and the cost` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- They do not: "these measures shall ensure a level of security appropriate to the risk presented".
#ASSERT (`Do my security measures ensure a level of security appropriate to the risk` WITH `my measures ensure a level of security appropriate to the risk presented, having regard to the state of the art and the cost` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P65: Have I given the calling subscriber the per-line possibility of hiding their number (Art 8(1))?
-- The possibility exists per line.
#ASSERT (`Have I given the calling subscriber the per-line possibility of hiding their number` WITH `the subscriber can prevent the presentation of the calling line identification` IS TRUE, `the possibility is on a per-line basis` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- It is only per call: the sentence asks for per-line.
#ASSERT (`Have I given the calling subscriber the per-line possibility of hiding their number` WITH `the subscriber can prevent the presentation of the calling line identification` IS TRUE, `the possibility is on a per-line basis` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- P66: After I override line identification to trace a malicious call, must I store the data and make it available (Art 10(a))?
-- After an override, the data will be stored and made available in accordance with national law.
#ASSERT (`After I override line identification to trace a malicious call must I store the data and make it available` WITH `I overrode the elimination of calling line identification to trace a malicious call` IS TRUE, `the storing is in accordance with national law` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No override: "In this case" does not reach it.
#ASSERT (`After I override line identification to trace a malicious call must I store the data and make it available` WITH `I overrode the elimination of calling line identification to trace a malicious call` IS FALSE, `the storing is in accordance with national law` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- P67: May a national authority audit my security measures and recommend best practice (Art 4(1a))?
-- Relevant national authorities shall be able to audit the measures and issue recommendations.
#ASSERT (`May a national authority audit my security measures and recommend best practice` WITH `the body is a relevant national authority` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a national authority: the sentence is silent.
#ASSERT (`May a national authority audit my security measures and recommend best practice` WITH `the body is a relevant national authority` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- P68: May the authority audit whether I complied with my notification duties (Art 4(4))?
-- The competent national authorities shall also be able to audit whether providers have complied.
#ASSERT (`May the authority audit whether I complied with my notification duties` WITH `the body is a competent national authority` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a competent national authority: the sentence is silent.
#ASSERT (`May the authority audit whether I complied with my notification duties` WITH `the body is a competent national authority` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

